                "retweet_count": 2,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "\ud83d\udea8 In a bipartisan vote this week, the House passed legislation containing my bill, the Permanent OPTN Fee Authority Act, a key reform designed to improve safety, transparency, and reliability for patients waiting for organ transplants. This bill was included as Section 8 of the \u201cMikaela Naylon Give Kids a Chance Act.\u201d\u00a0\n\u00a0\nThis is a critical step forward, and I\u2019ll continue working to stregthen our nation\u2019s organ transplant system.",
